# StockSage local settings — this file is copied to .env on first launch.
# .env is gitignored and stays on this machine. NEVER commit it.
#
# Easiest way to link Robinhood: use the form on the dashboard's Portfolio
# tab — it fills these in for you. Or edit .env by hand:

# Robinhood login (read-only portfolio access; StockSage never places orders)
ROBINHOOD_USERNAME=
ROBINHOOD_PASSWORD=

# Only if you use app-based two-factor auth: the TOTP setup key Robinhood
# showed when you configured your authenticator app (recommended: enable 2FA!)
#
# Know the trade-off before you fill this in. Storing the TOTP seed here lets
# scheduled runs sign in unattended — but it sits beside the password, so
# anything that can read this one file has both factors, and two-factor stops
# adding protection. Leave it blank and you keep a real second factor, at the
# cost of typing a code whenever the session expires (about weekly), which
# means scheduled publishes cannot refresh your holdings on their own.
# 'start.bat security' reports which way this is currently set.
ROBINHOOD_MFA_SECRET=

# Which brokerage account your trading routine acts on. Starred and shown
# first in the Portfolio tab. Your own account number — it stays in this
# gitignored file and never appears in the code or the repository.
# STOCKSAGE_AGENTIC_ACCOUNT=

# Optional overrides
# STOCKSAGE_DB=~/.stocksage/stocksage.db
